WEBVTT

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:03.770
DECEMBER 22, 2021

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:03.230
It's from...

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:05.230
ASUMI

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.230
- Asumi.
- Asumin.

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:28.290
If you give the CMD to Ran, the existence
of my conscience will be proven,

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:30.420
and my father will be accused for crimes.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:33.420
In the end, it will cancel the referendum.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:39.220
The KANAE System will be dismantled,
and the 24th Ward will return to the way it was.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:43.680
"Everyday life that is free,
but with no guarantees of safety."

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:52.190
If you give the CMD to my brother,
the bugs in Hazard Cast will be corrected,

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:53.940
and the ward referendum will proceed.

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:57.450
The KANAE System laws will take effect.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:01.330
Providing extremely thorough personal information
will become mandated,

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:08.750
and the 24th Ward will see "everyday life
with guaranteed safety at the cost of privacy."

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:14.630
Privacy that respects individuals,
or safety that deems everyone important...

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:17.470
The future of the 24th Ward.

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:23.140
RGB, the three of you need to choose.

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:28.150
Bye-bye.

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.400
Don't "bye-bye" me.

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:43.240
When she has that face,
there's no way I can choose a future.

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:47.290
I'm gonna go see Asumi!

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:48.670
What a coincidence.

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:50.500
Agreed 100%!

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.880
Asumin's location has to be there.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:55.460
I wonder where you pilfered that intel from?

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:01.850
Sorry I made you wait.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:04.430
Good timing, as always!

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:06.680
Let's see, here it is.

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:11.730
Be careful. The town is filled with SARG
trying to suppress the protestors.

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:13.070
Figures.

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:15.400
Ko, can we leave the driving to you?

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:18.740
Of course. I can predict
how SARG deployed their troops.

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:20.200
Shu!

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:22.120
Whoa, what?

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:24.870
Here. I was making these this past year.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:29.500
I had it completed.
I'm glad I can give it to you now.

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:33.920
Well, this is...

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:36.300
absolutely awesome.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:39.680
Now, get in!

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:41.970
We can't waste one second!

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:43.220
- Yep!
- Yeah!

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:49.940
In order to meet Asumin,
we need a special program.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:52.270
Right now, with the Cipher's boosting,

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:56.280
I can alter the basic data
Kunai left behind a lot faster.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:03:00.240
If we use this we'll be able to have
a direct conversation with Asumin.

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:03.780
This isn't right.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:06.950
Why are you trying to come see me?

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:10.210
I just contacted you to say goodbye.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:14.080
I don't want to see you guys anymore.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:18.050
If I see you, I...

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.810
What was that? So dangerous!

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:30.680
There's no driver.
That was autonomous driving.

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:32.440
Could that be Asumi?

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:33.730
Probably.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:37.940
The KANAE System is a broad system
that includes traffic systems as well.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:40.990
Seems like she really doesn't want us
to come visit, huh?

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:42.780
Seriously? That depresses me.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:44.950
Stubbornness runs in the blood.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:47.540
She's always been like that.

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:51.250
You never know her true feelings
until you get it out of her in person.

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:52.290
Yeah!

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:53.620
Shu!

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:55.710
I'm stopping that truck up ahead.

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:57.550
But how...

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:01.970
I sent you a map.

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:04.890
Look at it, and make sure
there won't be any damage in that area.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:06.600
There.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:13.690
So that's what this was about.

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:16.060
So reckless!

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:40.460
I don't want to determine everyone's future.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:45.300
I can't watch anymore stressful futures.

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:49.260
Please, just liberate me without coming here.

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:53.520
If I see you guys,
I'd be overflowing with regrets.

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:57.730
We're against the KANAE System referendum!

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:00.230
Return our Shantytown to us!

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:03.240
We'll march right into the mayor's office!

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:05.950
Kinako, look.

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:07.740
No way.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:08.950
Seriously?

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:10.870
It's not just Ran.

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:13.120
Koki, Shuta, and...

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:16.500
everyone in town!

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:19.960
They're all getting designated as terrorists.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:22.000
This is definitely wrong!

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:26.010
This is proof that the System BRAIN
is overflowing.

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:31.010
To stop this rampage, Gori Suido
has to put his pitchfork down.

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:33.100
Or else...

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:37.770
Mayor, are you planning on responding
to 0th's request for a conversation?

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:40.940
Not at all.

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:44.150
Civilians are being restrained
one after another on false charges.

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:46.990
Is Hazard Cast experiencing an abnormality?

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:50.570
I have not received such reports.

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:54.330
The KANAE System is perfect.

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:58.290
KANAE SYSTEM
BILL DELIBERATION BEGINS

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:58.290
That can't be...

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:01.210
Shuta is a terrorist?

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:05.170
Idiots! There's no way
Shu would do something like that!

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:07.630
That's right. All of this is weird.

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:10.640
Even Mr. Nakamura being asked to go
to the police station...

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:14.600
Maybe KANAE System
is all screwed up after all?

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:19.060
We should participate in the protest as well!

00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:21.360
Yeah!

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:24.780
- I'm gonna give them a piece of my mind!
- That's the spirit!

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:27.030
What about you, Mari?

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:31.990
I'll stay here
and wait for everyone to come back.

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:37.750
Terrorist! Stop right there!

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:39.960
If you don't stop, I'll shoot!

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:42.880
You're telling me to stop,

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:46.670
but there's no way I will!

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:54.890
I-I'll hit you with the next shot!

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:57.180
Ms. Hana!

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:09.860
You can't, RGB.

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:13.820
Please don't give me any more agony!

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:19.080
Damn it, the shutters are down!

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:23.130
<i>Mr. Koki.</i>

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:28.960
I've been listening to your situation.

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:30.260
<i>Sheesh.</i>

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:34.220
The control room cannot regain access
to the crime prevention system, either.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:38.180
I've been re-examining it
to see if there's a point of entry.

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:40.560
<i>Do you have the blueprints for the Cornucopia?</i>

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:47.270
<i>A perfect system doesn't exist.</i>

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:51.530
<i>As long as humans were behind the creation,
there should be an open seam somewhere.</i>

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:55.320
I see it!

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:00.910
If you go down the elevator shaft
that's under construction,

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:03.960
then go through
the trash disposal chute along the way,

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:06.840
we'll end up at the underground
materials import corridor.

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:12.470
You can go through the ventilation ducts
to arrive right in front of the Core Room!

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:14.550
Done!

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:15.970
Hurry!

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:20.770
They're so reckless.

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:25.940
But heroes always do reckless things.

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:32.190
The trash disposal chute should be right below.

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:34.160
Then, let's go!

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:35.160
Yeah!

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:46.960
Next up is the ventilation ducts
beyond the import corridor?

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:47.960
Yeah.

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:56.800
Why can't you just
quietly choose a future for me?

00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:01.220
I don't need any hope.

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:05.900
Because I learned that a future
where everyone is happy is just a dream!

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:12.530
<i>The person who taught a brat in Shantytown
that he has infinite possibilities was you, Asumin!</i>

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:14.820
<i>Choose from the tracks set for us?</i>

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:17.280
<i>That's not who we are!</i>

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:21.790
<i>Even if it looks impossible,
if we can face each other, talk it out,</i>

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:24.790
<i>and pool our wisdom, we can solve it.</i>

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:28.920
<i>So please meet with us
and let us hear your story!</i>

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:34.970
But I have to give up something.

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:37.930
Isn't that what it means to become an adult?

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:43.890
Another door.

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:46.230
The System Core is up ahead.

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:48.650
All right, I'm gonna break it open!

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:52.230
- Shu!
- Ow.

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:55.610
You're so reckless. However...

00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:59.490
Asumi, you're watching us, right?

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:02.580
We will not turn back until we see you!

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:09.040
That's right. As you know, little ol' me
can't finish my art without you, Asumin!

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:12.960
Asumi, you're scared of facing us
in person, aren't you?

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:19.430
However, you have the duty of facing
the foolish guys that you've affected!

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:23.560
This is a ritual for us to move forward!

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:26.140
You promised us when we were kids.

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:28.600
I'm your hero.

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:35.280
When you're in pain or when you're crying,
I'll rush over to you no matter how far I may be!

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:41.910
You finally gave up, huh?

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:51.210
Asumi!

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:56.130
What have they done to you?

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:07.350
- I'm in!
- Let's hurry.

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:10.100
Y-Yeah.

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:26.080
Gori Suido, come on stage and talk with me!

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:29.000
Hey 0th! Are you trying
to destroy the 24th Ward?

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:31.370
This is destruction for the sake of creation.

00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:34.920
This is not the world that Ms. Kanae wished for.

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:35.790
Why you...

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:37.420
Are you still pretending to be a hero?

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:39.630
Bring it!

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:43.590
Mayor! Please come down
and speak with the protestors!

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:46.260
At this rate, we don't know
when we'll have casualties.

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:49.310
That's a good thing for the referendum.

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:51.890
I can't believe it.

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:55.650
You weren't like this
when Ms. Kanae was still around!

00:11:56.150 --> 00:11:57.900
How dare you say that!

00:12:05.570 --> 00:12:06.700
Asumi?

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:11.370
Ran.

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:20.380
Miss Asumi.

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:26.350
If left alone, the KANAE System
will run further out of control.

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:30.520
I need to disappear or disperse myself.

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:33.850
I can't linger around forever.

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:36.440
I have to bid farewell to everyone.

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:37.690
That's not—

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:41.400
There's no other way! Isn't that right?

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:43.900
Well, yeah.

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:45.910
But we—

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:46.910
Stop it!

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:50.620
Please, don't torture me anymore!

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:55.420
<i>Accept it, or destroy it.
The future is one of those two.</i>

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:59.880
<i>No matter which future you choose,
I can't stay with everyone.</i>

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:05.680
<i>I'm no longer human.
I am the KANAE System itself.</i>

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:08.760
What happened in the 24th Ward's past,

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:10.680
what's happening right now,

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:12.390
and what will happen in the future...

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:15.060
I know everything!

00:13:15.390 --> 00:13:18.110
<i>Choosing the correct future</i>

00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:20.860
<i>means you abandon the mistaken future!</i>

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:23.570
<i>You choose the humans who can't be saved.</i>

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:26.280
<i>It's a task that someone has to do!</i>

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:27.660
It isn't!

00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:31.410
Such a responsibility is intolerable for humans.

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:34.790
I created the KANAE System
because it was intolerable!

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:40.960
And yet, I never imagined
Asumi's conscience still remained.

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:45.550
My physical body is already dead.

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:47.300
I can't return to what I was.

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:51.140
Meeting you and talking with you
is completely meaningless now.

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:53.390
Forget me!

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:56.350
I've been saying that this whole time,
so why did you come?

00:13:56.770 --> 00:14:00.110
Doing this only agonizes everyone!

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:17.540
I didn't know, either.

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:24.170
I want to see you, I want to talk to you,
I want to confirm that you're alive,

00:14:24.590 --> 00:14:27.550
I want to know
why you sent those Ciphers to us,

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:30.300
and I want to apologize about the fire...

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:35.930
My head was in a mess, all mixed up,
and I didn't understand anything.

00:14:36.310 --> 00:14:38.440
I hesitated on coming to see you,

00:14:39.100 --> 00:14:41.440
and I'm actually shaking right now.

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:45.190
But now that I see you, I finally understand.

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:49.700
You suffered so much by yourself
for everyone else's happiness.

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:54.790
Asumi, you suffered and agonized so much,
yet your face looks like that?

00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:58.790
I'm not convinced because of that!

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:03.750
We can take your place.

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:06.460
We won't shove this responsibility to anyone!

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:09.340
We will guide ourselves to our own futures!

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:15.260
And I'm saying such a burden shouldn't be
on all of your backs. That's impossible.

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:16.520
No.

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:20.940
Even if it's impossible for one person,
we will do it all together.

00:15:21.480 --> 00:15:27.030
Our future is something where everyone will give
their own opinions, and grasp it from within that.

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:33.070
But if you fail, you can't undo it!
It's too late if you've already lost something!

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:38.330
We'll likely fail. We'll lose something again.

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:42.670
But what's important is to accept the result,
no matter what happens.

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:47.590
With our own strength, we'll search to the very end
for a choice that we can be ready for.

00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:49.220
That's all there is to it.

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:51.260
But something like that...

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:54.510
We can do it.
No, we will make sure to do it.

00:15:54.970 --> 00:15:56.600
Yes, we can!

00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:01.940
We can make the impossible, possible.

00:16:14.740 --> 00:16:15.990
<i>I see.</i>

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:20.620
Such a future...

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:29.050
might be possible if it's RGB.

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:33.050
I wish I could've seen such a future with you.

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:35.050
Asumi.

00:16:38.470 --> 00:16:41.980
You understand, right? Asumi is already dead.

00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:43.390
We...

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:46.110
We came here to say goodbye.

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:47.440
No...

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:49.730
I don't want to!

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:55.410
I can't accept something like that.

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:57.490
I don't get it!

00:16:58.030 --> 00:17:01.370
Because I became a hero...

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:04.290
for you, Asumi.

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:08.540
Because it brought you joy.

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:11.590
Because it made you smile.

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:13.420
Shuta.

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:16.340
Thank you, Shuta.

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:22.100
You're smiling.

00:17:29.110 --> 00:17:30.150
Asumi!

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:33.360
I... I...

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:35.950
I love you!

00:17:40.530 --> 00:17:42.950
Yes. Me, too.

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:46.040
I love you too, Shuta.

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:49.590
What are you talking about?

00:17:49.840 --> 00:17:54.720
It's obvious that I love you more.
Isn't that right, Asumi?

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:56.630
Big Brother.

00:17:56.630 --> 00:17:58.510
Sheesh, you're so attached.

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:01.390
Little ol' me loves you too.

00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:04.020
My goddess of art.

00:18:04.020 --> 00:18:06.730
I can't ask for more from a subject of worship.

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:08.650
Ran.

00:18:09.060 --> 00:18:11.650
I can't ask more for words of love.

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:13.980
I love you too!

00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:18.990
Thanks to you, Asumi, I'm still alive.
Thank you!

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:24.660
I love you, too! You gave me the reason
to take my first step forward!

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:27.410
I love you.

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:29.580
I love you.

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:35.300
I love you. Asumi, I love you so much.

00:18:35.550 --> 00:18:36.720
I love you!

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:38.220
I love you.

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:41.010
Asumi, I love you!

00:18:41.010 --> 00:18:42.100
I love you.

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:43.680
I love you!

00:18:43.930 --> 00:18:46.310
I don't get it, but...

00:18:46.390 --> 00:18:48.640
- Yeah.
- I love you.

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:49.940
I love you!

00:18:50.230 --> 00:18:52.440
I love you.

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:53.980
I love you.

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:55.690
I love you.

00:18:57.610 --> 00:18:59.030
I love you!

00:19:03.830 --> 00:19:06.540
I love all of you, too!

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:09.210
But...

00:19:09.620 --> 00:19:12.040
I think I'm at my limit.

00:19:13.540 --> 00:19:17.880
Hey, my hero. Can I ask you for a favor?

00:19:18.880 --> 00:19:20.300
A favor?

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:24.350
I would like to say goodbye now.

00:19:27.310 --> 00:19:31.150
Is that really what you wish for?

00:19:34.060 --> 00:19:35.150
Yeah.

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:37.860
I've been watching you the whole time, Shuta.

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:41.070
You were so pathetic it was hard to watch.

00:19:42.160 --> 00:19:46.740
And I'd hate it
if you can't move forward because of me.

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:49.620
Shuta, you need to move on, too.

00:19:53.750 --> 00:19:55.000
Shuta.

00:19:55.630 --> 00:19:56.840
Shu.

00:19:59.590 --> 00:20:03.220
If you say that, then I...

00:20:07.970 --> 00:20:10.180
Goodbye, Asumi.

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:13.480
Goodbye, Shuta.

00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:45.260
Was that...

00:20:45.430 --> 00:20:48.310
Yeah. That was Ran and his friends.

00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:51.060
Everyone.

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:55.770
I would like to talk about the truth
behind the KANAE System.

00:20:59.900 --> 00:21:01.570
This is how it should be.

00:21:02.070 --> 00:21:03.650
Isn't that right?

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:06.280
Lady Kanae...

00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:12.790
APRIL 6, 2022

00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:21.130
Dad, I'm going to start attending
art school this year.

00:21:22.090 --> 00:21:24.590
I'll work hard, so please watch over me.

00:21:25.630 --> 00:21:27.050
It's done!

00:21:29.720 --> 00:21:30.890
Amazing!

00:21:31.220 --> 00:21:35.560
But this place is getting torn down
because of seismic resistance issues, right?

00:21:35.810 --> 00:21:40.770
Everything constantly changes.
Even Shantytown changes.

00:21:41.570 --> 00:21:44.860
And not everything is bad.

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:48.240
You're right!

00:21:49.580 --> 00:21:52.160
How was the homework I submitted?

00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:54.410
It was great, as I'd expect from you.

00:21:54.830 --> 00:22:00.710
<i>We weren't able to create a substitute system
for the previous KANAE System.</i>

00:22:00.920 --> 00:22:03.050
<i>That's why we relied on a biological brain.</i>

00:22:03.420 --> 00:22:07.010
<i>We humans will take its place.</i>

00:22:07.130 --> 00:22:11.720
<i>A reflection of open public opinion,
we have KANAE System version 2.0!</i>

00:22:12.060 --> 00:22:17.980
<i>It's not perfect, but we'll do our best.
That was Miss Asumi's last wish...</i>

00:22:18.350 --> 00:22:20.110
...and her desire.

00:22:20.650 --> 00:22:23.280
Little ol' us should live in that manner.

00:22:23.780 --> 00:22:24.610
Yo.

00:22:25.490 --> 00:22:28.490
Mr. Chikushi. Why are you here?

00:22:28.490 --> 00:22:30.370
I had a small errand.

00:22:30.620 --> 00:22:35.500
I heard you're transferring to your mother's
alma mater and getting a teaching license?

00:22:36.250 --> 00:22:38.420
I don't think that's a bad choice.

00:22:39.880 --> 00:22:42.880
Mr. Chikushi, you're all
police officers starting today, right?

00:22:43.130 --> 00:22:47.680
It's not my style, but I'll work as hard as I can.

00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:50.140
Koki, you should give your best, too.

00:22:51.010 --> 00:22:51.930
Okay.

00:22:53.350 --> 00:22:54.770
Hey, Mari.

00:22:54.770 --> 00:22:56.770
Do you think Shuta is doing well?

00:22:56.980 --> 00:22:59.480
Why are you asking me?

00:22:59.480 --> 00:23:02.150
You should contact him yourself.

00:23:02.480 --> 00:23:06.360
Well, he hardly ever contacts us, too.

00:23:07.150 --> 00:23:10.740
But no matter where he is, Shu is Shu.

00:23:12.120 --> 00:23:16.830
<i>The Far Eastern Special Administrative Region,
also known as the 24th Ward.</i>

00:23:18.080 --> 00:23:23.500
<i>It was successfully incorporated into Tokyo,
and its name was changed to "Nijimi Ward."</i>

00:23:24.590 --> 00:23:29.760
<i>Whether or not the people living there
can grasp happy futures is on their...</i>

00:23:30.300 --> 00:23:34.260
<i>no, on everyone's shoulders.</i>

00:23:39.850 --> 00:23:42.480
Hey, hand over all the cash you have! Huh?

00:23:45.860 --> 00:23:47.190
You're not hurt, are you?

00:23:49.490 --> 00:23:50.490
Want one?

00:23:51.450 --> 00:23:56.410
I baked this Golden Sunrise.
It's fresh out of the oven and delicious!

00:23:57.950 --> 00:23:59.910
FIN
